  "narrative": {
    "intro": "M C Dean recorded $449M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. M C Dean won 643 awards with an average award size of $699K, and obligations are up 7.4% year over year. M C Dean received the largest share of obligations from the Department of Defense with $293M, followed by the Department of Transportation with $61.5M and the Department of Justice with $47.8M. M C Dean’s work in Wired Telecommunications Carriers totaled $161M, and Engineering Services accounted for $109M. M C Dean also had significant obligations in Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) with $93.6M, and in Computer Systems Design Services with $28.2M. Fiscal-year totals show a steady rise to FY26, with prior-year obligations of $418M in FY25 and $308M in FY24. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest agency customers for M C Dean?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $293M. The Department of Transportation and the Department of Justice follow, obligating $61.5M and $47.8M respectively. The General Services Administration obligated $30.1M and the Department of Commerce obligated $6.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services generate the most obligations for M C Dean?",
        "body": "Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the largest market, generating $161M in obligations. Engineering Services generated $109M and Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) generated $93.6M. Computer Systems Design Services and Facilities Support Services generated $28.2M and $22.8M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does M C Dean make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "M C Dean has $449M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. M C Dean recorded 643 awards this fiscal year with an average award size of $699K, and obligations are up 7.4% year over year. Prior fiscal-year obligations were $418M in FY25, $308M in FY24, and earlier years as shown for trend context."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from M C Dean?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer from M C Dean, with $293M in obligations. The Department of Transportation obligated $61.5M and the Department of Justice obligated $47.8M. Other buyers include the General Services Administration at $30.1M and the Department of Commerce at $6.2M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does M C Dean sell to the government?",
      "a": "M C Dean sells telecommunications, engineering, security systems, and IT services to the government. Wired Telecommunications Carriers generated $161M and Engineering Services generated $109M. Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) generated $93.6M and Computer Systems Design Services generated $28.2M."
    },
